# ulx-extention-builder — Generation Rules

When creating or editing pages in this repo (especially from a **screenshot** or **user prompt**):

## Must follow

1. Read and apply `docs/UI-DESIGN-RULES.md` (spacing, typography, surfaces, patterns).
2. Read and apply `docs/PRIMEREACT-USAGE.md` (component mapping, size classes, form/drawer/dialog patterns).
3. Use **PrimeReact** for interactive UI (Button, InputText, Dropdown, Dialog, Sidebar, DataTable, Tag, etc.).
4. Use **Tailwind** only for layout/spacing/typography utilities.
5. Use theme tokens / classes (`bg-body`, `bg-surface`, `text-primary`, `border-border`, …) — do not hardcode product hex in JSX.
6. Prefer **content-only** pages for iframe upload (no full host chrome) unless the user asks for chrome.
7. Place new screens in `src/pages/`, register in `src/pages/manifest.mjs` (Home lists links; each route is a separate page).
8. Compile for upload with `npm run compile -- <path>` → output `dist/<path>/` (self-contained index.html + assets).
9. Keep pages content-only — no "All pages" / preview chrome inside page files. Local preview chrome is `AppPreviewShell` only.
10. Keep `src/pages/Home.jsx` as the clean page-index card (`ulx-extention-builder`) — do not embed other pages inside Home.
11. Use `PageLayout` and `PageHeader` for standard content-page structure.
12. Run `npm run validate` after adding or renaming a page.

## Screenshot / prompt workflow

1. Identify pattern: form settings | list/table | right drawer | confirm dialog.
2. Map each control to PrimeReact.
3. Apply kit spacing (page `p-6`/`p-8`, section gaps `mb-8`, field stacks `gap-4`, labels above inputs).
4. Use `m-size` / `l-size` for form controls.
5. Primary CTA: header right on list pages; drawer footer Done on the right, Close on the left; dialog actions right-aligned.

## Avoid

- Rebuilding ULS/ULX CSS inside the kit
- Cramped layouts, missing label hierarchy, raw unstyled HTML for buttons/inputs
- Marketing/hero layouts, purple gradients, decorative card grids for admin UIs
